WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.080
Knitting ribbing or adding both knit
and Pearl stitches to your knitting

00:00:06.146 --> 00:00:10.410
without a ribber means you
have to reform stitches.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.520
Now, that doesn't mean that you have
to just do boring ribbing,

00:00:13.586 --> 00:00:16.650
one by one or two by two ribbing.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.610
You can get very decorative
ribbing techniques on the ribber.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.890
Now, this is a pretty cabled pattern,
cabled ribbing pattern,

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.000
that's done completely on the machine.

00:00:30.066 --> 00:00:34.480
To work this pretty cable pattern,
it's just a two by two rib

00:00:34.546 --> 00:00:37.010
or knit two, Pearl two rib.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.250
You'll cast on and knit two rows.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.040
Now, set up your two by two ribbing

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.050
and then do a cable cross

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.650
on the opposite stitches.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:58.530
So for example, we've got knit and Pearl
stitches, every two row stitches here,

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:04.570
and on the Pearl stitch as they're
facing us will cross a single stitch.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:11.250
Now, knit two rows again,
reform those two stitches,

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:14.730
and create knit stitches
as they're facing you.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:19.610
Do your cable cross again, knit two rows,

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.370
and repeat for the length of your ribbing.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:27.250
So you're stopping every other row,
crossing your cables

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.133
and reforming your stitches.

00:01:29.533 --> 00:01:33.330
Now, try this technique because you'll
need to get into a rhythm

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.810
to create this stitch pattern.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:40.970
If your yarn is really slippery or you're
creating a really wide ribbing,

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:46.730
you might want to only knit the two rows,
do your cable cross, reform your stitches,

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:51.410
knit two rows,
do your cable cross, reform the stitches.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:56.920
If you also prefer, you can do your cable
crosses and reform all

00:01:56.986 --> 00:01:59.930
the stitches at the same time.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.530
A rhythm that you need
to set up for yourself.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:08.240
Try this technique just over a small
swatch, and you'll see what

00:02:08.306 --> 00:02:09.960
beautiful ribbing you can create.

